In EAP 7.4.*'s domain configuration if common profile is included in another profile like :

 
{code:java}
  <profile name="full-ha" includes="shared-profile"> {code}
 

the migration from EAP 7.4.* to EAP 8.0.0 fails with

 
{code:java}
 ERROR Migration failed: org.jboss.migration.core.ServerMigrationFailureException: org.jboss.migration.wfly10.config.management.ManagementOperationException: {"domain-failure-description" => {"WFLYCTL0062: Composite operation failed and was rolled back. Steps that failed:" => {"Operation step-16" => "WFLYHC0164: Profile 'full-ha' defines subsystem 'elytron' which is also defined in its ancestor profile 'shared-profile'. Overriding subsystems is not supported"}}}
:
Caused by: org.jboss.migration.wfly10.config.management.ManagementOperationException: {"domain-failure-description" => {"WFLYCTL0062: Composite operation failed and was rolled back. Steps that failed:" => {"Operation step-16" => "WFLYHC0164: Profile 'full-ha' defines subsystem 'elytron' which is also defined in its ancestor profile 'shared-profile'. Overriding subsystems is not supported"}}} {code}

Attaching domain.xml and host.xml . Is it a bug ?

